IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `eia-core`
IMPORT `ei2-nouns`

-- Employment Insurance Act (S.C. 1996, c. 23), ss 48 to 53: the claim procedure. Piece ei2. Text: the unofficial plain-text
-- rendering of the Justice Laws consolidation current to 2026-09-30. Seat: the claimant.
--
-- Relations (Hohfeld). s 48 and s 49(1): the claimant has the duty to claim and prove before the Commission is bound to
-- establish a benefit period or pay a week. s 48(3), s 49(3), s 51, s 52(2) and (4): the claimant's claim to a decision,
-- a notice, an opportunity to give information, and (s 52(4)) payment; the Commission's duty. s 49(2): the claimant's
-- claim to the benefit of the doubt; the Commission's duty. s 50: the Commission's power to require, and the claimant's
-- liability to the requirement and to losing entitlement while it is unmet (s 50(1)); s 50(10): the Commission's power to
-- waive, and the claimant's privilege thereby. s 52(1) and (5): the Commission's power to reconsider; the claimant's
-- liability to a reconsidered claim. s 53: the Commission's power to choose the manner of notice.
--
-- What the Commission "considers", "is satisfied of" or "is of the opinion" is a BOOLEAN input. The time for making a weekly
-- claim is "the prescribed time": regulation 26 (out of range: Regulations s 26, piece er2) sets it, so the last day on which
-- the claim could be made within it is a DATE input. The manner and form of a claim are the Commission's directions and
-- instructions: BOOLEAN inputs. Section 111 (reconsideration in general) is piece ei4's.
-- Ss 54 and 55(1) are regulation-making powers: inert machinery, see the coverage table.

§ `Section 48 - the initial claim`

-- (1): "No benefit period shall be established for a person unless the person makes an initial claim for benefits in accordance
-- with section 50 and the regulations and proves that the person is qualified to receive benefits." A necessary condition, not a
-- sufficient one (fork ei2-F16): the rule says when it is met. (When a benefit period is established is ss 9 and 10, piece ei1.)
-- src:926 | Claim required
-- src:927 | 48 (1) No benefit period shall be established for a person unless the person makes an initial claim for benefits in accordance with section 50 and the regulations and proves that the person is qualified to receive benefits.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 48(1) (src:926-927)
GIVEN `the person makes an initial claim for benefits in accordance with section 50 and the regulations` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person proves that the person is qualified to receive benefits` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 48(1) the first condition on which a benefit period may be established is met` IF
        `the person makes an initial claim for benefits in accordance with section 50 and the regulations`
    AND `the person proves that the person is qualified to receive benefits`

-- (2): "No benefit period shall be established unless the claimant supplies information in the form and manner directed by
-- the Commission, giving the claimant's employment circumstances and the circumstances pertaining to any interruption of
-- earnings, and such other information as the Commission may require."
-- src:928 | Information required
-- src:929 | (2) No benefit period shall be established unless the claimant supplies information in the form and manner directed by the Commission, giving the claimant’s employment circumstances and the circumstances pertaining to any interruption of earnings, and such other information as the Commission may require.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 48(2) (src:928-929)
GIVEN `the claimant supplies information in the form and manner directed by the Commission` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the information gives the claimant's employment circumstances` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the information gives the circumstances pertaining to any interruption of earnings` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Commission requires other information` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claimant supplies the other information the Commission requires` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 48(2) the second condition on which a benefit period may be established is met` IF
        `the claimant supplies information in the form and manner directed by the Commission`
    AND `the information gives the claimant's employment circumstances`
    AND `the information gives the circumstances pertaining to any interruption of earnings`
    AND ((NOT `the Commission requires other information`) OR `the claimant supplies the other information the Commission requires`)

-- (3): "On receiving an initial claim for benefits, the Commission shall decide whether the claimant is qualified to receive
-- benefits and notify the claimant of its decision." What the claimant is owed; TRUE when the Commission has done it.
-- src:930 | Notification
-- src:931 | (3) On receiving an initial claim for benefits, the Commission shall decide whether the claimant is qualified to receive benefits and notify the claimant of its decision.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 48(3) (src:930-931)
GIVEN `the Commission has received an initial claim for benefits` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Commission has decided whether the claimant is qualified to receive benefits` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Commission has notified the claimant of its decision` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 48(3) the Commission has done what it must on receiving the initial claim` IF
       (NOT `the Commission has received an initial claim for benefits`)
    OR (`the Commission has decided whether the claimant is qualified to receive benefits` AND `the Commission has notified the claimant of its decision`)

§ `Section 49 - proof for a week, and the benefit of the doubt`

-- (1): "A person is not entitled to receive benefits for a week of unemployment until the person makes a claim for benefits
-- for that week in accordance with section 50 and the regulations and proves that (a) the person meets the requirements for
-- receiving benefits; and (b) no circumstances or conditions exist that have the effect of disentitling or disqualifying the
-- person from receiving benefits." A necessary condition, as in s 48(1).
-- src:932 | Proof required
-- src:933 | 49 (1) A person is not entitled to receive benefits for a week of unemployment until the person makes a claim for benefits for that week in accordance with section 50 and the regulations and proves that
-- src:934 | (a) the person meets the requirements for receiving benefits; and
-- src:935 | (b) no circumstances or conditions exist that have the effect of disentitling or disqualifying the person from receiving benefits.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 49(1) (src:932-935)
GIVEN `the person makes a claim for benefits for that week in accordance with section 50 and the regulations` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person proves that the person meets the requirements for receiving benefits` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person proves that no circumstances or conditions exist that have the effect of disentitling or disqualifying the person from receiving benefits` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 49(1) the person has done what is needed to be entitled to receive benefits for the week` IF
        `the person makes a claim for benefits for that week in accordance with section 50 and the regulations`
    AND `the person proves that the person meets the requirements for receiving benefits`
    AND `the person proves that no circumstances or conditions exist that have the effect of disentitling or disqualifying the person from receiving benefits`

-- (2): "The Commission shall give the benefit of the doubt to the claimant on the issue of whether any circumstances or
-- conditions exist that have the effect of disqualifying the claimant under section 30 or disentitling the claimant under
-- section 31, 32 or 33, if the evidence on each side of the issue is equally balanced." JUST TRUE: the circumstance is
-- treated as not existing; NOTHING: the subsection does not apply. It composes with ss 30 to 33 by the caller treating a
-- JUST TRUE as "the circumstance does not exist".
-- src:936 | Benefit of the doubt
-- src:937 | (2) The Commission shall give the benefit of the doubt to the claimant on the issue of whether any circumstances or conditions exist that have the effect of disqualifying the claimant under section 30 or disentitling the claimant under section 31, 32 or 33, if the evidence on each side of the issue is equally balanced.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 49(2) (src:936-937)
GIVEN `the issue is whether circumstances or conditions exist that have the effect of disqualifying the claimant under section 30 or disentitling the claimant under section 31, 32 or 33` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the evidence on each side of the issue is equally balanced` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 49(2) the claimant is given the benefit of the doubt on the issue` IS
    IF     `the issue is whether circumstances or conditions exist that have the effect of disqualifying the claimant under section 30 or disentitling the claimant under section 31, 32 or 33`
       AND `the evidence on each side of the issue is equally balanced`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

-- (3): "On receiving a claim for benefits, the Commission shall decide whether benefits are payable to the claimant for that
-- week and notify the claimant of its decision."
-- src:938 | Notification
-- src:939 | (3) On receiving a claim for benefits, the Commission shall decide whether benefits are payable to the claimant for that week and notify the claimant of its decision.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 49(3) (src:938-939)
GIVEN `the Commission has received a claim for benefits for the week` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Commission has decided whether benefits are payable to the claimant for that week` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Commission has notified the claimant of its decision` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 49(3) the Commission has done what it must on receiving the claim for the week` IF
       (NOT `the Commission has received a claim for benefits for the week`)
    OR (`the Commission has decided whether benefits are payable to the claimant for that week` AND `the Commission has notified the claimant of its decision`)

§ `Section 50 - how a claim must be made, and what the Commission may require`

-- (2): "A claim for benefits shall be made in the manner directed at the office of the Commission that serves the area in which
-- the claimant resides, or at such other place as is prescribed or directed by the Commission."
-- src:942 | How a claim must be made
-- src:943 | (2) A claim for benefits shall be made in the manner directed at the office of the Commission that serves the area in which the claimant resides, or at such other place as is prescribed or directed by the Commission.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 50(2) (src:942-943)
GIVEN `the claim is made in the manner directed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claim is made at the office of the Commission that serves the area in which the claimant resides` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claim is made at another place prescribed or directed by the Commission` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 50(2) the claim is made as directed at the proper place` IF
        `the claim is made in the manner directed`
    AND (`the claim is made at the office of the Commission that serves the area in which the claimant resides` OR `the claim is made at another place prescribed or directed by the Commission`)

-- (3): "A claim for benefits shall be made by completing a form supplied or approved by the Commission, in the manner set out in
-- instructions of the Commission."
-- src:944 | Form
-- src:945 | (3) A claim for benefits shall be made by completing a form supplied or approved by the Commission, in the manner set out in instructions of the Commission.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 50(3) (src:944-945)
GIVEN `the claim is made by completing a form supplied or approved by the Commission` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the form is completed in the manner set out in instructions of the Commission` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 50(3) the claim is made on the proper form` IF
        `the claim is made by completing a form supplied or approved by the Commission`
    AND `the form is completed in the manner set out in instructions of the Commission`

-- (4): "A claim for benefits for a week of unemployment in a benefit period shall be made within the prescribed time." The
-- prescribed time is reg 26 (out of range: Regulations s 26, piece er2): three weeks after the week claimed, or one week after
-- it where the claimant has made no claim for four or more consecutive weeks. The last day on which a claim for the week
-- can be made within it is the input, and that day counts (the keel's fork F4).
-- src:946 | Time
-- src:947 | (4) A claim for benefits for a week of unemployment in a benefit period shall be made within the prescribed time.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 50(4) (src:946-947)
GIVEN `the day on which the claim for the week is made` IS A DATE
      `the last day on which a claim for that week can be made within the prescribed time` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 50(4) the claim for the week is made within the prescribed time` IF
    `the day on which the claim for the week is made` AT MOST `the last day on which a claim for that week can be made within the prescribed time`

-- (5), (6), (7), (8), (8.1): requirements the Commission "may" impose. Each is a power of the Commission and, once it is
-- exercised, a requirement under the section, which s 50(1) enforces; the rule says whether the requirement, if imposed, is
-- met. "Required" is the Commission's act; "complied" is the claimant's.
-- src:948 | Additional information
-- src:949 | (5) The Commission may at any time require a claimant to provide additional information about their claim for benefits.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 50(5) (src:948-949)
GIVEN `the Commission has required the claimant to provide additional information about the claim` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claimant has provided the additional information` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 50(5) the requirement to provide additional information is met` IF
       (NOT `the Commission has required the claimant to provide additional information about the claim`)
    OR `the claimant has provided the additional information`

-- src:950 | Making claim or providing information in person
-- src:951 | (6) The Commission may require a claimant or group or class of claimants to be at a suitable place at a suitable time in order to make a claim for benefits in person or provide additional information about a claim.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 50(6) (src:950-951)
GIVEN `the Commission has required the claimant or the group or class of claimants to be at a suitable place at a suitable time` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claimant has been at that place at that time to make the claim in person or provide additional information` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 50(6) the requirement to attend in person is met` IF
       (NOT `the Commission has required the claimant or the group or class of claimants to be at a suitable place at a suitable time`)
    OR `the claimant has been at that place at that time to make the claim in person or provide additional information`

-- src:952 | Registration for employment
-- src:953 | (7) For the purpose of proving that a claimant is available for work, the Commission may require the claimant to register for employment at an agency administered by the Government of Canada or a provincial government and to report to the agency at such reasonable times as the Commission or agency directs.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 50(7) (src:952-953)
GIVEN `the Commission has required the claimant to register for employment at an agency administered by the Government of Canada or a provincial government` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claimant has registered and reported to the agency at the reasonable times directed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 50(7) the requirement to register for employment is met` IF
       (NOT `the Commission has required the claimant to register for employment at an agency administered by the Government of Canada or a provincial government`)
    OR `the claimant has registered and reported to the agency at the reasonable times directed`

-- (8): the criteria for "reasonable and customary efforts" are the Regulations' (s 54(k.2); reg 9.001, piece er1).
-- src:954 | Proof of efforts to obtain employment
-- src:955 | (8) For the purpose of proving that a claimant is available for work and unable to obtain suitable employment, the Commission may require the claimant to prove that the claimant is making reasonable and customary efforts to obtain suitable employment.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 50(8) (src:954-955)
GIVEN `the Commission has required the claimant to prove that the claimant is making reasonable and customary efforts to obtain suitable employment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claimant has proved that the claimant is making reasonable and customary efforts to obtain suitable employment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 50(8) the requirement to prove efforts to obtain employment is met` IF
       (NOT `the Commission has required the claimant to prove that the claimant is making reasonable and customary efforts to obtain suitable employment`)
    OR `the claimant has proved that the claimant is making reasonable and customary efforts to obtain suitable employment`

-- src:956 | Proof — additional certificate
-- src:957 | (8.1) For the purpose of proving that the conditions of subsection 23.1(2) or 152.06(1) are met, the Commission may require the claimant to provide it with an additional certificate issued by a medical doctor or nurse practitioner.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 50(8.1) (src:956-957)
GIVEN `the Commission has required the claimant to provide an additional certificate issued by a medical doctor or nurse practitioner` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claimant has provided the additional certificate` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 50(8.1) the requirement to provide an additional certificate is met` IF
       (NOT `the Commission has required the claimant to provide an additional certificate issued by a medical doctor or nurse practitioner`)
    OR `the claimant has provided the additional certificate`

-- (9): "A claimant shall provide the mailing address of their normal place of residence, unless otherwise permitted by the
-- Commission."
-- src:958 | Mailing address
-- src:959 | (9) A claimant shall provide the mailing address of their normal place of residence, unless otherwise permitted by the Commission.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 50(9) (src:958-959)
GIVEN `the claimant has provided the mailing address of their normal place of residence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Commission has otherwise permitted` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 50(9) the requirement to provide a mailing address is met` IF
       `the claimant has provided the mailing address of their normal place of residence`
    OR `the Commission has otherwise permitted`

-- (10): "The Commission may waive or vary any of the conditions and requirements of this section or the regulations whenever in
-- its opinion the circumstances warrant the waiver or variation for the benefit of a claimant or a class or group of claimants."
-- src:960 | Waiver or variation of requirements
-- src:961 | (10) The Commission may waive or vary any of the conditions and requirements of this section or the regulations whenever in its opinion the circumstances warrant the waiver or variation for the benefit of a claimant or a class or group of claimants.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 50(10) (src:960-961)
GIVEN `in the opinion of the Commission the circumstances warrant the waiver or variation for the benefit of the claimant or a class or group of claimants` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 50(10) the Commission may waive or vary a condition or requirement` IF
    `in the opinion of the Commission the circumstances warrant the waiver or variation for the benefit of the claimant or a class or group of claimants`

-- (1): "A claimant who fails to fulfil or comply with a condition or requirement under this section is not entitled to receive
-- benefits for as long as the condition or requirement is not fulfilled or complied with." Each argument is "fulfilled or
-- complied with, or waived under subsection (10)".
-- src:940 | Entitlement to benefits
-- src:941 | 50 (1) A claimant who fails to fulfil or comply with a condition or requirement under this section is not entitled to receive benefits for as long as the condition or requirement is not fulfilled or complied with.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 50(1) (src:940-941)
GIVEN `the claim is made as directed at the proper place, or that is waived` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claim is made on the proper form, or that is waived` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claim for the week is made within the prescribed time, or that is waived` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the requirement to provide additional information is met, or waived` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the requirement to attend in person is met, or waived` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the requirement to register for employment is met, or waived` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the requirement to prove efforts to obtain employment is met, or waived` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the requirement to provide an additional certificate is met, or waived` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the requirement to provide a mailing address is met, or waived` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 50(1) the claimant is not entitled to receive benefits for as long as a condition or requirement is not met` IF
        NOT (    `the claim is made as directed at the proper place, or that is waived`
             AND `the claim is made on the proper form, or that is waived`
             AND `the claim for the week is made within the prescribed time, or that is waived`
             AND `the requirement to provide additional information is met, or waived`
             AND `the requirement to attend in person is met, or waived`
             AND `the requirement to register for employment is met, or waived`
             AND `the requirement to prove efforts to obtain employment is met, or waived`
             AND `the requirement to provide an additional certificate is met, or waived`
             AND `the requirement to provide a mailing address is met, or waived`)

§ `Sections 51 to 53 - information, reconsideration and notice`

-- 51: "If, in considering a claim for benefits, the Commission finds an indication from the documents relating to the claim
-- that the loss of employment resulted from the claimant's misconduct or that the claimant voluntarily left employment, the
-- Commission shall (a) give the claimant and the employer an opportunity to provide information as to the reasons for the loss
-- of employment; and (b) if the information is provided, take it into account in determining the claim."
-- src:962 | Information
-- src:963 | 51 If, in considering a claim for benefits, the Commission finds an indication from the documents relating to the claim that the loss of employment resulted from the claimant’s misconduct or that the claimant voluntarily left employment, the Commission shall
-- src:964 | (a) give the claimant and the employer an opportunity to provide information as to the reasons for the loss of employment; and
-- src:965 | (b) if the information is provided, take it into account in determining the claim.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 51 (src:962-965)
GIVEN `the Commission finds an indication from the documents relating to the claim that the loss of employment resulted from the claimant's misconduct or that the claimant voluntarily left employment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 51(a) the claimant and the employer are to be given an opportunity to provide information about the reasons for the loss of employment` IF
    `the Commission finds an indication from the documents relating to the claim that the loss of employment resulted from the claimant's misconduct or that the claimant voluntarily left employment`

-- src:962 | Information
-- src:963 | 51 If, in considering a claim for benefits, the Commission finds an indication from the documents relating to the claim that the loss of employment resulted from the claimant’s misconduct or that the claimant voluntarily left employment, the Commission shall
-- src:964 | (a) give the claimant and the employer an opportunity to provide information as to the reasons for the loss of employment; and
-- src:965 | (b) if the information is provided, take it into account in determining the claim.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 51(b) (src:962-965)
GIVEN `the Commission finds an indication from the documents relating to the claim that the loss of employment resulted from the claimant's misconduct or that the claimant voluntarily left employment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the information is provided` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 51(b) the Commission must take the information into account in determining the claim` IF
        `the Commission finds an indication from the documents relating to the claim that the loss of employment resulted from the claimant's misconduct or that the claimant voluntarily left employment`
    AND `the information is provided`

-- 52(1) and (5): "Despite section 111, but subject to subsection (5), the Commission may reconsider a claim for benefits within
-- 36 months after the benefits have been paid or would have been payable." "(5) If, in the opinion of the Commission, a false or
-- misleading statement or representation has been made in connection with a claim, the Commission has 72 months within which to
-- reconsider the claim." The last day of the 36 or 72 months counts (the keel's fork F4, and ei2-F10 here).
-- src:966 | Reconsideration of claim
-- src:967 | 52 (1) Despite section 111, but subject to subsection (5), the Commission may reconsider a claim for benefits within 36 months after the benefits have been paid or would have been payable.
-- src:976 | Extended time to reconsider claim
-- src:977 | (5) If, in the opinion of the Commission, a false or misleading statement or representation has been made in connection with a claim, the Commission has 72 months within which to reconsider the claim.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 52(1), s 52(5) (src:966-967) (src:976-977)
GIVEN `the day on which the benefits were paid or would have been payable` IS A DATE
      `in the opinion of the Commission a false or misleading statement or representation has been made in connection with the claim` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day on which the Commission would reconsider the claim` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 52(1) and (5) the Commission may reconsider the claim on the day` IF
    `the day on which the Commission would reconsider the claim` AT MOST (`add months` `the day on which the benefits were paid or would have been payable` (IF `in the opinion of the Commission a false or misleading statement or representation has been made in connection with the claim` THEN 72 ELSE 36))

-- 52(2): "If the Commission decides that a person has received money by way of benefits for which the person was not qualified or
-- to which the person was not entitled, or has not received money for which the person was qualified and to which the person
-- was entitled, the Commission must calculate the amount of the money and notify the claimant of its decision."
-- src:968 | Decision
-- src:969 | (2) If the Commission decides that a person has received money by way of benefits for which the person was not qualified or to which the person was not entitled, or has not received money for which the person was qualified and to which the person was entitled, the Commission must calculate the amount of the money and notify the claimant of its decision.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 52(2) (src:968-969)
GIVEN `the Commission decides that the person has received money by way of benefits for which the person was not qualified or to which the person was not entitled` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Commission decides that the person has not received money for which the person was qualified and to which the person was entitled` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 52(2) the Commission must calculate the amount of the money and notify the claimant of its decision` IF
       `the Commission decides that the person has received money by way of benefits for which the person was not qualified or to which the person was not entitled`
    OR `the Commission decides that the person has not received money for which the person was qualified and to which the person was entitled`

-- 52(3): "(a) the amount calculated is repayable under section 43; and (b) the day that the Commission notifies the person of
-- the amount is, for the purposes of subsection 47(3), the day on which the liability arises."
-- src:970 | Amount repayable
-- src:971 | (3) If the Commission decides that a person has received money by way of benefits for which the person was not qualified or to which the person was not entitled,
-- src:972 | (a) the amount calculated is repayable under section 43; and
-- src:973 | (b) the day that the Commission notifies the person of the amount is, for the purposes of subsection 47(3), the day on which the liability arises.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 52(3)(a) (src:970-972)
GIVEN `the Commission decides that the person has received money by way of benefits for which the person was not qualified or to which the person was not entitled` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 52(3)(a) the amount calculated is repayable under section 43` IS
    IF `the Commission decides that the person has received money by way of benefits for which the person was not qualified or to which the person was not entitled`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:970 | Amount repayable
-- src:971 | (3) If the Commission decides that a person has received money by way of benefits for which the person was not qualified or to which the person was not entitled,
-- src:972 | (a) the amount calculated is repayable under section 43; and
-- src:973 | (b) the day that the Commission notifies the person of the amount is, for the purposes of subsection 47(3), the day on which the liability arises.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 52(3)(b) (src:970-973)
GIVEN `the Commission decides that the person has received money by way of benefits for which the person was not qualified or to which the person was not entitled` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day on which the Commission notifies the person of the amount` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `s 52(3)(b) the day on which the liability arises for the purposes of subsection 47(3)` IS
    IF `the Commission decides that the person has received money by way of benefits for which the person was not qualified or to which the person was not entitled`
    THEN JUST `the day on which the Commission notifies the person of the amount`
    ELSE NOTHING

-- 52(4): "If the Commission decides that a person was qualified and entitled to receive money by way of benefits, and the money
-- was not paid, the amount calculated is payable to the claimant." The claimant's claim: JUST the amount, else NOTHING.
-- src:974 | Amount payable
-- src:975 | (4) If the Commission decides that a person was qualified and entitled to receive money by way of benefits, and the money was not paid, the amount calculated is payable to the claimant.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 52(4) (src:974-975)
GIVEN `the Commission decides that the person was qualified and entitled to receive money by way of benefits` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the money was not paid` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the amount calculated` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `s 52(4) the amount payable to the claimant` IS
    IF     `the Commission decides that the person was qualified and entitled to receive money by way of benefits`
       AND `the money was not paid`
    THEN JUST `the amount calculated`
    ELSE NOTHING

-- 53: "If the Commission is required to notify a person of a decision under this Part, it may have that person notified in such
-- manner as it considers adequate." The manner is the Commission's to choose: a BOOLEAN input, "it considers the manner adequate".
-- src:978 | Notification
-- src:979 | 53 If the Commission is required to notify a person of a decision under this Part, it may have that person notified in such manner as it considers adequate.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 53 (src:978-979)
GIVEN `the Commission is required to notify the person of a decision under Part I` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Commission considers the manner of notice adequate` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 53 the person may be notified in that manner` IF
        `the Commission is required to notify the person of a decision under Part I`
    AND `the Commission considers the manner of notice adequate`
